# 1. PROJECT IDENTITY

Application name: ForenX

Full title: Cross-Platform Browser Artifact Forensics and Evidence Validation Workbench

Category: Digital Forensics / Browser Artifact Analysis / Evidence Integrity

Primary users:
- Digital forensics students
- Digital forensic investigators
- Cybersecurity researchers
- Incident response analysts
- Academic research teams

Primary purpose:

ForenX enables an investigator to import authorized browser artifact databases, preserve evidence metadata, calculate SHA-256 hashes, extract supported browser activity, normalize timestamps, construct a unified event timeline, validate extracted results against known test data, and export traceable investigation reports.

The application must work on Windows and Linux.

The primary deployment model is local-first. Case data and evidence must remain on the investigator's computer unless the investigator explicitly chooses an export destination.

ForenX is an academic forensic workbench, not a certified forensic acquisition suite. Do not claim legal admissibility, forensic certification, complete browser coverage, or guaranteed recovery of deleted data.

